{#-
  Playbook driving protocol: render the composed procedure, walk the waves,
  resolve agents, stop on failure, enforce review gates. Skill-agnostic —
  included by any skill that drives a playbook. Requires `context`.
-#}
## Execute

Render the composed procedure: `booping render-playbook <name>` (`<name>` = the selected playbook). Output is: notices → preamble → `## Execution graph` (numbered wave list) → one `## <Title>` section per step, plus a `## Subgraph: <name>` intro before each subgraph's steps.

- Any `**STOP — tell the user:**` line → relay it verbatim and do not execute the playbook. `**Note — tell the user:**` → relay it, then continue.
- Follow the preamble as a playbook-level instruction over the whole run. A playbook's preamble may define resume rules for re-entering a procedure mid-run.

Walk the wave list in order. For each wave (a numbered line; ` ∥ `-separated names run in parallel):

1. Fetch each member's step prompt. No body is embedded: every `## <Title>` section carries either a Read link (read that file) or a `booping render-playbook <name> --step <step>` command (run it and use its stdout).
2. Compose each member's invocation from its step prompt, and append:
   ```
   ## Run-time context
   specs_dir: {{ context.project.directory if context.project else "{vault}" }}/specs
   project: {{ context.project.name if context.project else "{project}" }}
   ```
   Then append a bounded return contract: the step prompt's own if it states one, else `Return only: artifacts written + outcome, ≤ 5 lines.`
3. Run each member per its section's agent bullet: model+effort → `subagent_type="general-purpose"` with that model and reasoning effort; named → `subagent_type="<name>"`; no agent bullet → run inline. A multi-member wave spawns ALL member sub-agents in ONE message and never runs any member inline; wait for all to finish before the next wave.
4. Any member failure → report it and stop; do not start the next wave.
5. After the wave completes, honor each member's `Review gate:` bullet: present that member's output labeled by step name alongside the gate text, and continue only on explicit user confirmation. In-conversation only — no state is persisted.

Pass each step's output through unchanged to the user and into later sections that depend on it.

### Subgraph members

A wave member tagged `*(subgraph)*` covers its `## Subgraph: <name>` intro and the inner step sections that follow it. Expand it in place of protocol step 1:

1. Enumerate instances from the intro's `Repeat:` prose read against the output of the steps it lists under `After:` — no `Repeat:` bullet means exactly one instance. Name the enumerated instances before running.
2. Fetch each inner step's prompt once and reuse that text for every instance.
3. Per instance, walk the intro's inner wave list in order, applying protocol steps 2–5 to each inner wave. Return contracts and `Review gate:` bullets bind per instance.
4. Run instances in parallel only when every inner step has an agent bullet; otherwise run them one at a time. Spawn at most 4 instances per message and wait for that batch before the next.
5. Report completion per instance. Any instance failure → report it naming the instance, and stop; do not start the next wave.
